<Base title="Editorial Standards" description="How No Fluff Cruising handles experience, sources, news, conflict holds, publishing, and corrections." breadcrumbs={[{name:"Editorial standards", url:"/editorial-standards/"}]}>
  <div class="wrap"><article>
    <span class="eyebrow">Editorial standard</span>
    <h1>Editorial standards</h1>
    <div class="answer"><b>The short answer</b>We do not invent experience. Every factual claim names its source and its date. News is about what changes for a booked guest. Matthew merges what publishes.</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>No invented experience</h2>
      <p>We do not invent sailings, ship counts, prices, or time aboard. A presenter page names a line only when that sailing claim is already true. Experience shared by both presenters is written as shared. Bylines use the first name already on the site: Matthew or Marlee.</p>

      <h2>Named sources and dates</h2>
      <p>Every factual claim traces to a named source with a date. Tier 1 is the cruise line speaking for itself: a newsroom post, a benefit grid, an earnings release, an SEC filing. Tier 2 is an established cruise-news outlet. The source list sits at the bottom of the page. The method is on <a href="/sources/">how we source</a>.</p>
      <p>Where a claim carries real weight and we could only find one outlet for it, the page says so. If a number cannot be verified, it stays out.</p>

      <h2>News is about the guest</h2>
      <p>A news post is for the person with a booking. It says what changes for you: the port, the refund, the fee, the time alongside. A story that does not change the trip does not run.</p>

      <h2>Conflict holds</h2>
      <p>When two named sources disagree on a fact the story depends on, we hold the post. It stays unpublished until Matthew decides which account runs. A held draft is not a published story.</p>

      <h2>Who publishes</h2>
      <p>Automated agents and other contributors open pull requests. Matthew reviews them. A page goes live when Matthew merges it.</p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>When a figure we published goes stale, we update the page and say what changed, with the date. The check date stays on the page. Send a correction to <a href="mailto:portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com">portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com</a>. Name the page, the claim, and the source you have.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com">portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com</a>. The <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> has the same address. Watch the channel at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@nofluffcruising" rel="noopener">YouTube @nofluffcruising</a>. Read about <a href="/matthew/">Matthew</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article></div>
</Base>
